title: $:/mf/gen/CLI command/mf log rollback
catalog: CLI command
target: mf log rollback
summary: Go back to a time: revert your changes since then (not the watcher's)

!! Reference

```
Go back to a time: revert your changes since then (not the watcher's)

Usage: mf log rollback [OPTIONS] <ARGS>...

Arguments:
  <ARGS>...
          [plan] TIME: a duration ago (30m, 2h, 1d), ISO-8601 in UTC, or @<unix-ms>

Options:
      --metadata-only
          Leave out the operations needing a filesystem action

      --on-move-available <ON_MOVE_AVAILABLE>
          Policy when the file is present: apply|skip|abort|ask (default apply)

      --on-move-unavailable <ON_MOVE_UNAVAILABLE>
          Policy when the file is missing: apply|skip|abort|ask (default ask)

      --force
          Skip the confirmation prompt

      --silent
          Suppress informational output

  -h, --help
          Print help
```
